PAGE Explanation
LAYERS 1 1
LAYER 1 1 0 Main
GRAVITY 1.00
ON 1
LABEL 48.00 36.00 DOSING VIBRATOR - PLASTIC PELLETS LOADED BY SUCTION FROM A BIG BAG\nExample: vacuum loading + vibrator dosing, with circuit, chart and flow chart
LABEL 48.00 100.00 1) PROCESS (page 1)\n Big Bag (feeder, 3000 pellets) drops pellets into the bag discharge.\n Suction lance (suction head) pulls pellets up the vacuum line.\n VP01 vacuum pump (blower) carries them to the vacuum receiver.\n Receiver drop outlet: pellets fall i
LABEL 48.00 250.00 2) CIRCUIT (page 2)\n SB1 start (latched by K1), SB0 stop (normally closed).\n K1 = system RUN relay. T1 = flasher timer: vacuum 20 s ON / 8 s OFF.\n KM1 = vacuum pump contactor -> CT1 current -> motor M1 runs VP01.\n S2 = dosing enable switch. KM2 = vibrator
LABEL 48.00 410.00 3) FLOW CHART (page 3)\n It reads K1, KM1, KM2 and shows the path of the scan in yellow.\n Green decision = true (ON). Grey box = branch not taken.\n Tags ST_SUCTION / ST_REST / ST_DOSING / ST_DOSEOFF / ST_STOP\n show the state. The displays show KM1, KM2, CT
LABEL 48.00 540.00 4) HOW TO RUN\n 1. Press Run. Go to page 2 and press SB1 (START).\n 2. Watch page 1: pellets travel Big Bag > receiver > hopper > process.\n 3. Watch page 2: lamps, currents and the trend. Page 3: flow chart.\n 4. Press SB0 to stop. Turn S2 off to stop only t
LABEL 48.00 690.00 TIP: the Big Bag holds 3000 units. When the feeder is empty, reload the example.
